vscode: Alt+click six times, type the dash
open: release.md

@brief
Eight times: turn the six lines under the heading into a markdown
bullet list by putting `- ` in front of each one.

Block, `I`, type, `Esc`. Nothing to think about.

@keys
| `Ctrl-V` | start a block |
| `I` | insert at the left edge on every line |

@hints
`2j` from the top puts you on the first item. `Ctrl-V`, `5j`, `I- `,
`Esc`.
--
Do not look at the other lines while typing. They change on `Esc`, not
before.

@solution
    2 j Ctrl-V 5 j I -<Space> <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Thirteen keystrokes. By the last rep the `Esc` should feel like the
key that does the work, because it is.

@start release.md
# Release 2024.03

Refund window enforced at thirty days
Order cutoff moved to 14:00 UTC
Payment capture retries with backoff
Customer email on refund issued
Reconcile export includes currency
Registry split into domain and infrastructure

@expected release.md
# Release 2024.03

- Refund window enforced at thirty days
- Order cutoff moved to 14:00 UTC
- Payment capture retries with backoff
- Customer email on refund issued
- Reconcile export includes currency
- Registry split into domain and infrastructure
